Rewritten 2026-07-06 as an unordered backlog; completed work and its
rationale live in the git history of this file, docs/design/, and NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Every item has an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md,
and the planning/implementation/review process (who plans, who
implements, who reviews, which gates run) is docs/plans/README.md.
"window: pre-release" marks items whose cheap form expires when 1.0-0
freezes the R and dbarts.h compatibility contracts: they need a
go/no-go decision before submission, not necessarily the work itself.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  architecture-doc: LANDED - docs/architecture.md (the contributor
    orientation; five-question comprehension check passed). Awaiting
    VD's skim for wrongness; plan file has the landing record.
  blocked-jacobi-trees: exact parallel tree updates via noise-splitting
    augmentation (per-tree pseudo-responses y_k ~ N(g_k, sigma^2/b),
    sum-constrained): b trees update independently per barrier at the
    cost of b-fold precision on structure moves. Candidate mechanism
    for within-chain-threading; an ESS-per-second experiment decides.
  data-ownership: own predictor storage instead of borrowing REAL(x)
    (drops the PROT_* pinning and the const_cast write-through);
    changes the documented aliasing of per-observation updates.
    window: pre-release.
  gpu-bart: MEMO LANDED (docs/design/gpu-bart.md, d0f737a) plus the
    frontier companion (docs/design/parallel-bart-frontier.md).
    Falsifiers 1-3 REPORTED (2026-07-08, parallel-falsifiers): 3.4 and
    3.2a both SURVIVE (E2 field share 82-88% => DRAM drop ~6x; E1 atoms
    2-4 orders below n at b in {4,8}; E3 agreement 0.97, survivor
    0.07-0.12). Both flagship CPU candidates live. Backend-seam design
    still waits on items 4-5 (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes).
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: XBART-style root-down tree sampling on the
    provisioned cut-scan kernel; the highest-ceiling large-n item and
    the realistic doorway to any GPU backend. MEMO + KERNEL LANDED
    2026-07-08 (grow-from-root.md; driver benchmarks/kernels/
    grow_from_root.c). Cut-scan measured on M1 Max: seq root scan
    histogram-bound ~13.6 GB/s (not DRAM-bound), scattered-leaf scan
    DRAM/cache-line-bound ~0.7x the 52 GB/s roofline; multiplier
    scan-vs-single-cut ~p on a scattered leaf (10x p=10, 53x p=50),
    ~p/4 root-order. Recommendation: GO on the shared scan primitive
    and grow-from-root as a WARM-START producer (feeds installTrees/
    warm.start, sidesteps validity); NO-GO on shipping it as a
    standalone posterior sampler - the exact-sampler use of the scan
    belongs to frontier 3.1's informed proposal. Awaiting VD approval
    of the follow-up "grow-from-root warm-start producer" (shares the
    scan primitive with frontier item 4).
  hot-layer-u8: FOLDED into data-ownership's owned container (VD
    2026-07-07, after phase-1 kernel measurements showed no standalone
    partition win); per-column widths land with the container and get
    re-measured end-to-end there.
  interaction-constraints: structured sparsity and interaction limits
    on the SplitSelector seam. consumer-gated.
  monotone-bart: shape-constrained fits via the tree-level leaf-draw
    hook the design provisioned.
  multi-forest-models: multinomial, heteroscedastic, hurdle - the BCF
    two-forest machinery (forest-split-bcf, complete at c9fd2fe) is
    the template; one design note each when picked.
  moves-degenerate-root-guard: correctness-audit block-1 finding. A
    single-node tree with no available split variable forces a birth
    (drawBirthableNode's hasSingleNode branch skips the availability
    check) and drawRuleForVariable then reads data.types[(size_t)-1];
    the death branch is equally unguarded. Latent (constant columns
    still quantize to >= 1 cut; the veto rejects those births) but
    reachable via zero-cut columns, e.g. setCutPoints on a root-only
    sampler. Fix: such a tree's move is a no-op; guard both branches.
    Small, engine, neutral on non-degenerate data.
  mutation-journal: build-new-and-swap for setPredictor instead of
    copy-old-and-restore; cell-granular journal for the patch paths;
    document the cost contract per entry point.
  negative-binomial: count outcomes via the Polya-Gamma NB
    augmentation (the PG sampler already ships); the r update decides
    integer vs real shape - a caveat shared with weighted-binary.
  ordinal-outcomes: cumulative probit on the existing truncated-normal
    machinery plus a cutpoint block.
  parallel-falsifiers: DONE 2026-07-08. Measured verdicts on frontier
    falsifiers 1-3 (field-fraction profile, atom census, stale-residual
    agreement), kill conditions applied. Both SURVIVE: 3.4 (E1 + E2 both
    clear; field ~85%, atoms << n at b in {4,8}) and 3.2a (agreement
    0.97, survivor 0.07-0.12). See docs/design/parallel-bart-frontier.md
    section 5 and docs/plans/parallel-falsifiers.md Status; driver
    benchmarks/R/parallel-falsifiers.R. Instrumentation reverted, not
    landed. Successors: frontier items 4-5.
  pointwise-loglik: per-observation log-likelihood as a Results field
    (null-skip), unlocking loo/WAIC integration.
  prior-predictive: R-level verbs over the already-ported prior
    sampling entry points, for prior calibration workflows.
  retrospective-reviews: GREENLIT program of six reviews (correctness
    derivation audit, interface, gate blind spots, SBC calibration,
    field roadmap survey, architecture critique + numerical
    robustness), strictly sequential; order and scope in the plan
    file. IN PROGRESS 2026-07-08: review 1 running as
    correctness-audit (paired independent derivers per formula
    block).
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge; a pybind11 facade wrapper becomes prototype-scale. horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. decision-gated.
  rbart-loop-profile: CLOSED 2026-07-07. The callback rewrite landed
    (rbart-loop-fix, 55ce4ba, bitwise-neutral) but reclaimed nothing:
    the round trip was never the cost - the overhead over the in-core
    floor is the R-side Gibbs blocks (O(n) group means, the tau
    slice's per-draw optim). Moving those into C atop the callback
    entry is the unpicked follow-up; tables in both plan files. (The
    correctness bug the measurement surfaced was fixed as
    rbart-custom-prior-divergence, c7fa0e4.)
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Remaining: PR-gate the
    sanitizers workflow once the new gcc-asan/valgrind legs prove
    stable on pushes; optional codecov badge (VD's call); optional
    roxygen2 and NEWS.md migrations (do not start unasked).
  robust-errors: Student-t residuals as a scale-mixture on the
    workingWeights hook; composes with user weights.
  sparse-extensions: in-place mutation, sparse x.test, streaming range
    kernel, mutation on dense-backed mixed columns (sparse-columns.md
    landing notes). The u8 width entry moved to hot-layer-u8.
    consumer-gated.
  survival-models: AFT log-normal (censoring via truncated-normal
    latents; riAFTBART is the named consumer) and discrete-time hazard
    (person-period ingestion); the design note picks which lands first.
  warm-starts: LANDED 933eed8 (installTrees + bart2 warm.start;
    same-grid v1, cross-grid refused). Remaining stretch: the
    cross-grid remap over mapOldCutPointsOntoNew; reopen when a
    consumer needs new-data warm starts.
  weighted-binary: integer-weight probit (exact via replicated latent
    draws, linear in total counts; threshold hybrid if that matters)
    and arbitrary real logistic weights (needs a real-shape PG sampler;
    IPW use is a pseudo-likelihood trap). decision-gated, post 1.0.
  within-chain-threading: previously assessed-and-deferred pending
    n >= 1e5 workloads, now confirmed common. Deterministic fixed-block
    reductions preserve thread-count invariance; the measurement
    interacts with hot-layer-u8 (same DRAM-bound regime) and competes
    with blocked-jacobi-trees as the mechanism.
  x86-simd: three linalg SSE2/AVX bodies are scalar with intrinsics
    commented out (predates the rewrite; the originals used
    non-temporal stores autovectorization cannot emit) - measure on
    x86, restore or delete; add misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant to the
    dispatch table; SSR SIMD leaf; Windows-arm64 NEON config.

